165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (   On behalf of the Health Department of the Akmola Region and the administration of Kokshetau Higher Medical College, we extend our heartfelt greetings to all professionals in the fields of medical education and oncology attending this important conference, dedicated to the 75th anniversary of our college and to pressing issues in oncology within the framework of the 13th Regional Meeting of the Asia-Pacific Organization for Cancer Prevention \(APOCP\).    This event holds special significance as it takes place during a milestone year for our college. We celebrate this anniversary with a profound sense of responsibility for the future. For the medical community of the Akmola Region, this international conference is of strategic importance. Today, Kokshetau is rapidly developing as a center for advanced oncological care, uniting specialized clinics, scientific research, and educational programs into a unified medical cluster. This integration not only allows us to implement modern diagnostic and treatment methods but also to train highly qualified professionals capable of responding to the challenges of oncology.   We sincerely thank all guests, speakers, and organizers for their participation in this meaningful event. Your knowledge, experience, and willingness to share innovative solutions make this conference a truly valuable platform for professional dialogue.    On behalf of the college leadership and staff, we wish all participants fruitful work, engaging scientific discussions, new discoveries, and effective collaborative projects. May this forum serve as a powerful impetus for the development of the regional oncology service and contribute to improving the quality of life for our patients.)
/E (   On behalf of the Health Department of the Akmola Region and the administration of Kokshetau Higher Medical College, we extend our heartfelt greetings to all professionals in the fields of medical education and oncology attending this important conference, dedicated to the 75th anniversary of our college and to pressing issues in oncology within the framework of the 13th Regional Meeting of the Asia-Pacific Organization for Cancer Prevention \(APOCP\).    This event holds special significance as it takes place during a milestone year for our college. We celebrate this anniversary with a profound sense of responsibility for the future. For the medical community of the Akmola Region, this international conference is of strategic importance. Today, Kokshetau is rapidly developing as a center for advanced oncological care, uniting specialized clinics, scientific research, and educational programs into a unified medical cluster. This integration not only allows us to implement modern diagnostic and treatment methods but also to train highly qualified professionals capable of responding to the challenges of oncology.   We sincerely thank all guests, speakers, and organizers for their participation in this meaningful event. Your knowledge, experience, and willingness to share innovative solutions make this conference a truly valuable platform for professional dialogue.    On behalf of the college leadership and staff, we wish all participants fruitful work, engaging scientific discussions, new discoveries, and effective collaborative projects. May this forum serve as a powerful impetus for the development of the regional oncology service and contribute to improving the quality of life for our patients.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2 3 4]
>>
endobj
